# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
#
# Intentionally EMPTY. This file suppresses *fixable* CVEs we consciously accept;
# there are currently none.
#
# - Fixable base-image CVEs are patched at build time by `apt-get upgrade` in the
#   Dockerfiles, so they never reach the scan.
# - Unfixable base CVEs (no upstream patch — e.g. perl-base, kernel headers,
#   ncurses) are skipped by the CI Trivy job's `ignore-unfixed: true`, so they do
#   not need explicit entries here.
#
# Add an entry (with a dated justification) only for a CVE that HAS a fix but that
# we deliberately choose not to apply yet.
